# /etc/predigol/app.env - the APPLICATION's settings (FBI_*), handed to the API, the worker and one-off commands.
# root:root, chmod 600. NEVER in Git, never in a chat. Database URLs are NOT here: docker-compose.yml builds one
# per role from the server's env file.

# ── API-Football (the worker) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY_ACTION: rotación recomendada posteriormente. A new key goes only here.
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_KEY=
# The REAL plan of the account, and our own daily ceiling below its limit.
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_PLAN=ultra
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_DAILY_BUDGET=60000
FBI_APIFOOTBALL_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# Requests by endpoint, lane and job (plan PM, PM-01-02; docs/owner/PM_01_02_CONSUMO_POR_ENDPOINT.md): counted in memory where the daily
# budget is spent and added to raw.provider_endpoint_usage once a minute; the limiter also keeps each day's per-minute peaks in
# raw.provider_minute_daily. It measures only: no request, answer or page changes. ON without the line; 0/off/false/no switches it
# off (the worker and the one-off commands read it when they start).
# FBI_PROVIDER_USAGE=on
# The sweeps nobody reads, trimmed (plan PM, PM-04-03, BE-062; docs/owner/PM_04_03_RECORTES_DE_BARRIDOS.md): /predictions once a match,
# /teams/statistics weekly for all, /players monthly on each competition's own day, the squad round spread over the week. No field
# any page shows is lost. Off by default (1/on/true/yes turns it on); the worker reads it when it calls each sweep.
# FBI_REFERENCE_TRIMS=off
# The reference as deep as each competition's level and priority (plan PM, PM-04-04, BE-063; docs/owner/PM_04_04_PROFUNDIDAD_REFERENCIA.md):
# completa (P0/P1, or level A/B) asks what it asks today; media (level C) drops trophies, past absences and careers; minima (level D,
# or not measured yet, without P0/P1) asks only the squad and the coach; /players only for P0-P2 and never minima. Reads the nightly
# matrix (PM-02-03) once an hour. Off by default (everything completa); the worker reads it when it calls each sweep.
# FBI_REFERENCE_DEPTH=off
# The lanes of the daily budget (plan PM, PM-04-01, BE-060; docs/owner/PM_04_CARRILES_DEL_CUPO.md): each job's lane has a daily
# ceiling. off (default) = the behaviour before the lanes, exactly; measure = decide and log what would have been refused
# (quota.lane_would_limit), refuse nothing; enforce = refuse a lane past its ceiling (the job stops as on a spent budget). Needs
# FBI_PROVIDER_USAGE on (it reads those counts). Ceilings: lane=N pairs over the table in fbi/providers/lanes.py. The worker reads them
# when it starts: change with a dated copy of app.env and `predigolctl up`.
# FBI_APIFOOTBALL_LANES=off
# FBI_APIFOOTBALL_LANE_CEILINGS=
# Dynamic limits over the lanes (plan PM, PM-04-02, BE-061; same guide): on = at 60 % of the budget the fills (históricos,
# ampliación, reparación, sin carril) pause, at 75 % the reference, at 88 % only directo, cuotas, alineaciones and resultados go
# on; the last EMERGENCY_RESERVE requests are theirs alone; no fill between 03:50 and 05:00 UTC. Acts only while the lanes are
# measure or enforce; off by default. The worker reads them when it starts.
# FBI_APIFOOTBALL_DYNAMIC_LIMITS=off
# FBI_APIFOOTBALL_EMERGENCY_RESERVE=7000
# The account's pause (plan PM, PM-04-02, BE-061, the correction of PM-01-03): an error about the ACCOUNT inside an HTTP 200 (out of
# requests for the day, a paid account answered as the free plan, a key refused) stops every request of the process for the pause,
# then one request tries again. ON without the line; 0/off/false/no = the behaviour before (each such answer is a plain error).
# FBI_APIFOOTBALL_ACCOUNT_GUARD=on
# FBI_APIFOOTBALL_ACCOUNT_PAUSE_SECONDS=900
# The catalogue watch (plan PM, PM-03-08, DOC-010; docs/owner/EXPANSION_P3.md section 8): after the daily catalogue_refresh, a new league
# id of a priority country or a new season of a discontinued or cyclical competition (config/catalogue_watch.yaml) is logged as
# catalogue_watch.finding and noted in the run. 0 requests. Off by default (1/on/true/yes turns it on); read at each refresh.
# FBI_CATALOGUE_WATCH=off

# Odds capture windows tuned on the laptop (pushed with deploy/cutover/push-app-env.sh); empty = the defaults.
# FBI_ODDS_PREMATCH_WINDOWS=
# FBI_ODDS_NEARCLOSE_WINDOW=
# FBI_ODDS_WINDOW_TOLERANCE=
# The current-price book of the odds explorer (plan Cuotas, BE-010; docs/owner/CUOTAS_LIBRO_VIGENTE_BE010.md): the worker rebuilds
# market.book_current from RAW every 10 min. Off = anything but 1/on/true/yes. It asks the provider nothing and nothing of the
# models, the picks or the parlay reads it; the worker needs a restart to read it.
# FBI_ODDS_BOOK=0
# The book refreshes (plan Cuotas, BE-011; docs/owner/CUOTAS_REFRESCOS_Y_API_BE011.md): /odds asked again between the model
# windows for the explorer's book only (nothing the models, the picks or the parlay read). Needs FBI_ODDS_BOOK on too; its own
# daily budget inside the shared quota, cut before any other job. Off = anything but 1/on/true/yes; the worker needs a restart.
# FBI_ODDS_BOOK_REFRESH=0
# FBI_ODDS_BOOK_DAILY_BUDGET=8000
# FBI_ODDS_BOOK_RESERVE=6000
# The web shows the new Cuotas explorer instead of the current page (GET /auth/me -> odds_explorer). Off until verified in
# production; the API must be recreated to read it.
# FBI_ODDS_EXPLORER=0
# Where the Picks board takes its decision from (plan PICKS, F3; BE-014). `intelligence` = the newest decision-v1 row of each
# selection (calibrated probability, EV, state) instead of the pick engine's raw numbers. Off = anything but exactly
# `intelligence`. It can only take cards away from a reader (the board's rules AND Intelligence must both recommend); it changes
# no decision, model or settlement. The API must be recreated to read it.
# FBI_PICKS_SOURCE=legacy

# ── Sign-in ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# (generated) 32 random bytes, base64: encrypts the second-factor secrets and keys the recovery codes. The API
# refuses to start without it. Losing it means every account sets its authenticator up again.
FBI_AUTH_SECRET_KEY=
# Roles that must use a second factor (TOTP: Google / Microsoft Authenticator).
FBI_AUTH_MFA_ROLES=SUPER_ADMIN

# ── Notices (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Telegram bot for the app's own notices and for the server monitor (bin/healthcheck.sh).
FBI_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
FBI_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# off: the owner's chat gets no notice of shadow picks nor of their settlement (UX-023, P14). Set it BEFORE the token above.
FBI_NOTIFY_PICKS=on
# Owner's communiqués (UX-022): the public channel (@name or id; the bot must be its administrator), the secret in the
# bot's webhook path (24+ random characters) and the most communiqués published in a day. Everything works without Telegram.
FBI_TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_ID=
FBI_ANNOUNCE_DAILY_CAP=3
# The bot's webhook secret goes in the path of its address; leave it empty and the bot's welcome is off.
FBI_TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Errors of the API and the worker to Sentry (free Developer plan): the DSN of a project created by the owner.
# Empty = off. Nothing personal is sent (no cookies, bodies, IPs, users or local variables): fbi/core/sentry.py.
FBI_SENTRY_DSN=
# The web project's DSN (plan UX, A2; docs/owner/OBSERVABILIDAD_UX_A2.md): it stays on the server - the browser sends its events to the
# API's tunnel (POST /api/v1/monitoring/envelope) and the API forwards them. Empty = the tunnel drops them. A secret, as the line above.
FBI_SENTRY_WEB_DSN=
# The environment tag of both projects; FBI_ENV (production on the server) while absent.
# FBI_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# What the tunnel lets through, per minute and client / per hour and process / per day and process (the web's errors are few and the free
# plan has 5,000 a month). The defaults are the ones shown.
# FBI_MONITORING_RATE_LIMIT=20
# FBI_MONITORING_HOURLY_CAP=10
# FBI_MONITORING_DAILY_CAP=20
# Load times (LCP, INP, CLS) have their own, smaller share per API process (closing plan 5.3); past it they are dropped
# FBI_MONITORING_VITALS_HOURLY_CAP=2
# FBI_MONITORING_VITALS_DAILY_CAP=6
# The synthetic journey (every 15 minutes: sign in as a reader, read Inicio, a match and Picks; it alerts the owner when it breaks): the
# public origin and a dedicated READER account (no second factor) the owner creates, never a real person's and never SUPER_ADMIN. The
# account is exempt from the consent gate, the e-mails and the analytics. Empty = the journey does not run. The password is written only in
# the server's own app.env (root, 600; docs/owner/OBSERVABILIDAD_UX_A2.md, 6.3), never in this file, Git or a chat.
# FBI_SYNTHETIC_BASE_URL=https://example.com
# FBI_SYNTHETIC_EMAIL=
# FBI_SYNTHETIC_PASSWORD=

# ── E-mail to readers (plan UX, A5; docs/owner/EMAIL_MENSAJERIA_UX_A5.md) ────────────────────────────────
# The messenger (its own container, with the API's database role) sends the queue through Resend. Born OFF: with
# FBI_EMAIL_SEND=0 the queue fills and nothing leaves. On only after the owner's P2 (Resend: the sending subdomain,
# a key restricted to sending, the webhook's secret) and P3 (SPF, DKIM, DMARC) pass a real test to Gmail and Outlook.
# The messenger needs a restart to read these; the API reads the webhook's secret (no secret: no webhook, 404).
# FBI_EMAIL_SEND=0
# The sender on the authenticated subdomain, e.g. PrediGol <avisos@correo.example.com>; a reply-to is optional.
FBI_EMAIL_FROM=
# FBI_EMAIL_REPLY_TO=
# Secrets: the sending key (re_...) and the webhook's signing secret (whsec_...).
FBI_RESEND_API_KEY=
FBI_RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Messages handed to Resend per UTC day (Free: 100 a day, received e-mails included).
# FBI_EMAIL_DAILY_CAP=90

# ── Getting in without the owner (plan UX, A7; docs/owner/CUENTA_ACCESO_UX_A7.md) ─────────────────────────
# Invitations by e-mail and recovering the password or unlocking the account with a one-use link (only its hash is
# kept), plus the notices of a new sign-in and of security changes. Born OFF: with FBI_SELF_SERVICE=0 those routes do
# not exist, the console creates accounts with a temporary password as before and no such e-mail is queued. On only
# after FBI_EMAIL_SEND=1 has passed its real test; the API and the messenger read it (restart both). Rollback: 0
# again - links already sent stop working; accounts already invited or deleted stay as they are.
# FBI_SELF_SERVICE=0
# The links' rows, 30 days after they were used or expired: dry = the messenger only counts them; on = deletes them.
# FBI_LINKS_PURGE=dry

# ── Membership (plan UX, A8; docs/owner/MEMBRESIA_UX_A8.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# A trial when an account is activated, periods the owner records in the console (payment and extend, courtesy,
# suspension, «will not renew») and the notices before and at the end. Born OFF: with FBI_MEMBERSHIP_ENFORCE=0 an
# ended membership limits nothing (everybody keeps full access; the states are still shown). On only once every live
# account has its period. The API reads it (restart). Rollback: 0 again - periods and payments stay.
# FBI_MEMBERSHIP_ENFORCE=0
# The trial of a new account, 7 to 20 days (the invitation can say otherwise for one account).
# FBI_TRIAL_DAYS=20
# P6 of the plan: the currency the console proposes for a payment.
# FBI_MEMBERSHIP_CURRENCY=COP
# The price of the single plan, per month, said in the profile's Membership section: one amount per currency, and
# the reader pays in whichever they choose. 0 (or off) hides that currency. Changing a price changes what is said
# from then on; the periods and payments already recorded do not change. The API reads it (restart).
# FBI_MEMBERSHIP_PRICE_COP=150000
# FBI_MEMBERSHIP_PRICE_USD=50
# Discounts (UX-005). The owner's coupons are made in the console (Usuarios -> Cupones), with no setting. The loyalty
# discount: the percentage off every payment of a reader who has paid for FBI_LOYALTY_AFTER_MONTHS months or more (20 and
# 2: «más de dos meses»; a trial or a courtesy is not a month paid). 0 or off turns it off. A coupon and loyalty never
# add up: the larger applies. Nothing is charged by PrediGol: the owner records the payment and the discount with it.
# The API reads them (restart).
# FBI_LOYALTY_PERCENT=20
# FBI_LOYALTY_AFTER_MONTHS=2
# P7 of the plan: the WhatsApp Business number readers write to for renewing (digits with the country code). Empty:
# the notices say to answer the e-mail (FBI_EMAIL_REPLY_TO) or to look in the profile.
# FBI_SUPPORT_WHATSAPP=
# Closing plan 4.2: which ways to reach PrediGol the app offers and in what order (comma list of whatsapp, tickets, email;
# absent: the three in that order; one that is named but not available is left out) and the hours someone answers, in
# plain words (up to 80 characters). The API reads them (restart): changing them touches no code.
# FBI_SUPPORT_CHANNELS=whatsapp,tickets,email
# FBI_SUPPORT_HOURS=Lun-Vie 9:00-18:00, hora de Bogotá

# Plan maestro UX/UI 2026 («Noche de partido»): what it added is born off. Each is read by the API (recreate it to read a
# change) and shown by the web only when GET /auth/me says so; none changes a pick, a price, a model or a membership.
# «Estado de los precios» (/odds/status) and its link from Cuotas (decision 4).
# FBI_ODDS_STATUS=0
# The assistant of Ayuda: it answers only with the content of Ayuda and the glossary, never about a pick or a bet.
# FBI_HELP_ASSISTANT=0
# The official Telegram channel shown in Ayuda's contact: a public https://t.me/... link. It shows only with the link AND
# `telegram` named in FBI_SUPPORT_CHANNELS; without the link the channel is left out.
# FBI_TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_URL=
# The Noticias section (/news) and its entry in «Más» (decision 2). Only with real news being read (FBI_NEWS_USERS on).
# FBI_NEWS_FEED=0
# «Avisos», the reader's inbox (/inbox) and the bell (decision 1): what was already sent to the reader, with read marks.
# Needs migration 0137.
# FBI_INBOX=0

# ── Consent and product analytics (plan UX, A4 and A6; docs/owner/ANALITICA_UX_A6.md) ─────────────────────────────────
# FBI_CONSENT_GATE: the four boxes (terms, data processing, +18, the risk notice) a reader ticks at the first sign-in and again when a
# MATERIAL version of a text replaces the one accepted. Born OFF: nobody is asked until the lawyer (P5) has reviewed the texts and a
# version with draft=false is published (backend/src/fbi/customer/texts/versions.json). 1 turns it on and only works once no required text
# is a draft; "drafts" turns it on regardless and is for QA, NEVER for production. SUPER_ADMIN and the synthetic account are exempt.
# FBI_CONSENT_GATE=1
# FBI_PRODUCT_EVENTS: the closed catalog of the readers' events (what was opened, saved or followed; a pseudonym, no IP, no free text).
#   off      nothing is recorded (the default)
#   consent  only the readers whose latest "analytics" consent is granted (the most prudent mode)
#   on       every reader (only if the lawyer says a separate box is not needed)
# FBI_PRODUCT_EVENTS=off
# The raw events are kept 90 days and the daily totals 13 months, but they are deleted only with FBI_EVENTS_PURGE=on: dry (the default)
# counts what would go and deletes nothing; off keeps everything. The same switch governs the retention of the feedback, the notices and
# the customer states (B6, B7, B11).
# FBI_EVENTS_PURGE=dry
# The owner's view of the events shows global figures only from this many active readers (default 20), and the browser may send at most
# FBI_EVENTS_RATE_LIMIT events a minute per client (default 120).
# FBI_PRODUCT_MIN_SUBJECTS=20
# FBI_EVENTS_RATE_LIMIT=120

# ── AI decision layer (fbi.ai, docs/ai/AI_DECISION_LAYER.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# shadow = evaluation: it analyses, reviews and records, and changes nothing users see. Never "enforce" without
# the owner's decision after the shadow gate passes. off = no AI at all (the free, rules-only part keeps running).
FBI_AI_MODE=shadow
# One model per level: L1 economical (every match with a market), L2 intermediate (candidates, escalated matches),
# L3 strong (the best candidates, the picks of the day, parlay legs, contradictions). provider:model.
FBI_AI_MODEL_BULK=anthropic:claude-haiku-5-5
FBI_AI_MODEL_ANALYSIS=anthropic:claude-sonnet-5-5
FBI_AI_MODEL_FINAL=anthropic:claude-opus-5-5
# The month's hard cap (US$) and the daily target it adapts around (busier days spend more, never past the month).
# PrediGol Intelligence (13 Oct 2026): US$180 a month, alerts at 50 / 70 / 85 / 95 / 100 %; one cap for the whole layer.
FBI_AI_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=180
FBI_AI_DAILY_TARGET_USD=6.00
FBI_AI_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=6.00
FBI_AI_MAX_LLM_REVIEWS_PER_DAY=90
FBI_AI_MAX_DEEP_PER_DAY=15
# Keys (secrets): Anthropic for the models, Exa for the web research. Empty = that part is off.
# FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC is the key of the PREDIGOL workspace (worker-prod); FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC_LAB is the LAB workspace's own key
# (worker-lab), read only by the LAB's probes and tests, never by production (docs/owner/IA_ACCIONES_MANUALES.md, actions 5 to 7).
FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC=
FBI_AI_KEY_ANTHROPIC_LAB=
EXA_API_KEY=
# The multi-agent engines in SHADOW (Plan Maestro IA, phase 3; fbi.ai.arms): LAB workspace only, and nothing they write reaches a user or the
# decision layer. They run only when ALL THREE words below say so; with any one at its default (the values shown) nothing runs. The worker
# needs a restart to read them. To go back: FBI_AI_ENGINES=rules,llm and FBI_AI_SHADOW_SAMPLE=0.
# Engines: rules and llm are always there (FBI_AI_MODE governs them); the list can only add ma-v1, ma-v1-h and cs-v1 (COUNCIL SOLO).
# The plan's activation is rules,llm,ma-v1,ma-v1-h.
# FBI_AI_ENGINES=rules,llm
# The share of the matches with candidates the shadow runs on, from 0 to 1 (0.3 = 30 %); each match is assigned once and keeps its group.
# FBI_AI_SHADOW_SAMPLE=0
# The agents that may run: match and council. The plan's activation is match,council.
# FBI_AI_AGENTS=
# How often the worker looks for matches to run the shadow on (the ai_orchestrate job; default 5, minimum 1). Without the three words above it does nothing.
# FBI_AI_ORCHESTRATE_MINUTES=5
# After the result (Plan Maestro IA, phase 5): both off by default; they write only into tables no pick, filter, decision or user reads. The worker needs a
# restart to read them. 1 switches on, 0 goes back.
# The mechanical attribution of the shadow and the Post-Match Reviewer (pmr-v1, Batch, LAB), in the daily step ai_learn (07:35 Bogota).
# FBI_AI_PM_REVIEWER=0
# The Learning Analyst (la-v1, Batch, LAB), on Mondays in intel_weekly: it only proposes hypotheses per agent version.
# FBI_AI_LEARNING_ANALYST=0

# ── The readers' narrative (plan UX, A11, docs/owner/NARRATIVA_UX_A11.md) ─────────────────────────────────
# The structured reading of a match written as prose in ES and EN by the bulk model from the reading's own facts, checked sentence by
# sentence before a reader sees it. Its OWN budget, apart from Intelligence's above (ai.user_usage, never ai.usage): 0 or absent = it
# never spends; the owner's P8 approves US$30. The worker and the API read the switch at start: off (absent) | shadow (the worker writes,
# only the Admin Console's preview shows - review a sample first) | on (readers see it). =0 or off stops it without a deploy.
# FBI_AI_USER_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=30
# FBI_USER_NARRATIVE=shadow
# FBI_USER_NARRATIVE_MINUTES=10
# The post-match review of the chronicle (IA-022/023, no model, no cost): on by default; =0 stops it without a deploy (the rows stay).
# FBI_CHRONICLE_REVIEW=1
# FBI_CHRONICLE_REVIEW_MINUTES=60
# The single chronicle's companions (IA-116..119, docs/owner/IA_116_..IA_119_*.md), no model, no cost, nothing a reader sees:
# the update after the official line-up and the why of each selection (off | shadow), the rule of stock phrases and repetitions
# (shadow measures | on drops | off), the factual review after the match (off | shadow). The worker reads them at start.
# FBI_CHRONICLE_LINEUP=off
# FBI_CHRONICLE_REPEAT=shadow
# FBI_CHRONICLE_REVIEW_V2=off
# The chronicle's statistics from C-13 (Plan Maestro PM, PM-11-07; IA-158; fbi.chronicle.stat_sheet): off by default (the chronicle is
# then what it was). =on: the expected goals the single chronicle may tell come from the team's statistics document (analytics.stat_documents,
# the match's competition season, u10 / all, the figure its profile shows), the packet's xG is left out and the form keeps no per-match
# average. The worker reads it at start; =off goes back without a deploy. Before turning it on: python -m scripts.chronicle_stat_check check
# (0 differences in 500 matches) and the worker's memory measured before and after.
# FBI_CHRONICLE_STAT_SHEET=off

# ── «Cómo le va a PrediGol» (plan UX, A12, docs/owner/TRANSPARENCIA_UX_A12.md) ──────────────────────────────
# The track record for signed-in readers: the published picks with their sample, the days without picks and why, the line value,
# the forecast's calibration and what is in evaluation (counts only). OFF while absent: the owner reviews it first at /transparency
# with the owner's account (the console's preview, P9); =1 opens it to readers (the API recreated). Each deploy checks every figure
# against an independent query (python -m scripts.transparency_check).
# FBI_TRANSPARENCY=1

# ── The welcome and the favourites (plan UX, A13; docs/owner/ONBOARDING_UX_A13.md) ──────────────────────
# Both ON while absent (the plan approved them; the lines turn them off without a deploy, the API recreated):
# FBI_ONBOARDING=0 sends every account straight to Inicio (no welcome; the favourites stay);
# FBI_PERSONALIZATION=0 gives every reader the common Inicio (the leagues suggested for Colombia), whatever they follow.
# FBI_ONBOARDING=0
# FBI_PERSONALIZATION=0

# ── El recorrido de bienvenida y las guías de cada pantalla (UX-032; docs/owner/GUIAS_BIENVENIDA_UX_032.md) ──
# ON while absent (the owner approved the plan); =0 stops the page from showing any guide - the tour, the first visit to each
# screen and the first guide of Perfil - without a deploy (the API recreated). What each reader has seen stays recorded.
# FBI_GUIDES=0

# ── Ayuda y soporte (plan UX, A14; docs/owner/AYUDA_SOPORTE_UX_A14.md) ───────────────────────────────────────
# A reader's tickets - «Reportar un problema» in Ayuda, in an error and in a match - with their context, answered from the
# console's Soporte (/admin/support). ON while absent (the plan approved it); =0 takes the tickets away without a deploy (the
# API recreated): Ayuda, its contact (FBI_SUPPORT_WHATSAPP of A8, FBI_EMAIL_REPLY_TO of A5) and the privacy requests stay, and
# the tickets already written can still be read and answered.
# FBI_SUPPORT=0

# ── Feedback y Novedades (plan UX, B6; docs/owner/FEEDBACK_UX_B6.md) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The monthly survey («¿Qué tan útil te resultó PrediGol este mes?», at most once every 30 days, after a useful moment, never
# in an account's first week) and «¿Te sirvió?» at the end of a reading or an explanation. ON while absent (the plan approved
# it); =0 takes both away without a deploy (the API recreated) - the answers stay, Novedades stays. The answers older than 24
# months follow the product events' retention switch (FBI_EVENTS_PURGE: dry while absent - counted, nothing deleted -, off or on).
# FBI_FEEDBACK=0

# ── Avisos en el dispositivo (plan UX, B7; docs/owner/AVISOS_UX_B7.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web Push with PrediGol's own VAPID key: the result of what a reader saved, their teams' line-ups, the day's summary, a
# reminder they asked for (the bell) and their account - with quiet hours (22:00-08:00, their zone), at most 3 a day and
# categories they switch off. ON while FBI_PUSH is absent (the plan approved it) BUT nothing is offered or sent until the
# owner sets the key (P12): FBI_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, made on the server into a root-only file (never onto the screen) with
#   sudo sh -c 'umask 077; docker exec predigol-api python -m scripts.vapid_keys > /root/predigol-vapid.txt'
# and its first line appended to /etc/predigol/app.env (root, 600 - the file that already holds the second factor's key);
# never in a chat. Every step: docs/owner/AVISOS_UX_B7.md, section 9.
# FBI_PUSH=0 stops the sending and hides every invitation without a deploy (the API and the messenger recreated).
# FBI_VAPID_SUBJECT: the contact the push services see (mailto: or https:); FBI_WEB_BASE_URL while absent.
# FBI_PUSH=0
# FBI_VAPID_SUBJECT=
# The private key's line, appended by the steps of section 9 and never typed or shown (empty here, as every secret of this file):
# FBI_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# FBI_PUSH_SERVICE_HOSTS is for QA's stand-in push service only: never in production.

# ── Email opcional: el resumen semanal (plan UX, B8; docs/owner/EMAIL_OPCIONAL_UX_B8.md) ─────────────────────────────
# Commercial e-mail, only to the readers who ask for it in their profile (an optional consent, never ticked beforehand),
# left in one click from any summary (RFC 8058) or in the profile. Born OFF, and it needs the e-mail on (FBI_EMAIL_SEND=1,
# A5) AND its own sender on ANOTHER domain than FBI_EMAIL_FROM's - e.g. PrediGol <resumen@novedades.example.com>, with its
# SPF, DKIM and DMARC in P3 - so that a summary marked as spam never drags the account's e-mails down. While any of the
# three is missing the profile does not offer it and nothing is queued. The API and the messenger read them (recreate
# both). Rollback: FBI_DIGEST=0 - nothing more is queued and nothing queued leaves; the readers' choices stay.
# FBI_DIGEST=0
# FBI_DIGEST_FROM=
# Summaries queued a day at most (under the queue's own FBI_EMAIL_DAILY_CAP; Resend Free sends 100 a day).
# FBI_DIGEST_DAILY_CAP=30

# ── PrediGol's forecast of each match (plan F5, docs/owner/PRONOSTICO_F5.md) ────────────────────────────
# A probability and its interval per core market, apart from the value (needs a price) and from any pick. Written by the pick
# pipeline, read by the match page and Home. Every signed-in account sees it since plan UX A9 (the owner approved it; the line
# absent = on): FBI_FORECAST_USERS=0 hides it again without a deploy (the API needs a restart to read it). A value that is neither
# 1/on/true/yes nor empty counts as off. The Admin Console's preview always shows it.
# FBI_FORECAST_USERS=1
# FBI_MATCH_FORECAST=0 stops the pipeline from writing new forecasts without a deploy (the worker needs a restart). What was written
# stays; hide it from users with FBI_FORECAST_USERS=0. Default on.
# FBI_MATCH_FORECAST=1
# FBI_FORECAST_SEAL: the stable calibration seal (AD-B03, IA-073, docs/owner/IA_073_SELLO_DE_CALIBRACION.md). shadow (the default in
# code) also writes forecast-v1-seal beside forecast-v1, read by no reader; off stops writing it (the worker needs a restart).
# FBI_FORECAST_SEAL=shadow
# FBI_SCENARIOS: the scenarios engine (AD-B02, IA-082, docs/owner/IA_082_MOTOR_DE_ESCENARIOS.md). off (the default in code) writes
# nothing; shadow makes the worker append, every 6 hours, one reading per live coded competition to intel.scenario_readings, read by
# no reader (the worker needs a restart).
# FBI_SCENARIOS=off

# ── What readers are shown (plans F4 and F7; on since plan UX A9 and A10, docs/owner/VALOR_DIARIO_UX_A9.md) ──
# The line absent = on: the owner approved showing them with A9 and A10. =0 hides one again without a deploy (the API needs a restart to
# read these); a value that is neither 1/on/true/yes nor empty counts as off. The Admin Console's preview always shows them.
# FBI_CALENDAR_USERS=1    the calendar of a match: both teams' last and next matches and days of rest (F4, docs/owner/CALENDARIO_F4.md)
# FBI_KNOWLEDGE_USERS=1   the "Postpartido" block of a finished match: what happened, layer by layer (F7, docs/owner/POSTPARTIDO_F7.md)
# FBI_READING_USERS=1     the structured reading of a match: six sections of facts with their references, no AI (A9)
# FBI_NEWS_USERS=1        the news of a match and Home's «Noticias»: verified items with their source, status and link (A10,
#                         docs/owner/NOTICIAS_UX_A10.md); never an article's text
# FBI_EXPLAIN=1         «Explícame»: the frequent questions of a match, a pick and the parlay answered from what PrediGol already
#                         keeps - no AI (B9, docs/owner/EXPLICAME_UX_B9.md); 0 removes the buttons, the API answers 404 explain_off
# FBI_LIFECYCLE=1       each customer's state of the day (invited, activated, habitual, at risk, expiring, renewed, expired) with its
#                         reasons, computed by the messenger once a day (B11, docs/owner/CICLO_VIDA_UX_B11.md); 0 stops the
#                         calculation and keeps the history
# Switches of the worker (it needs a restart to read them). On by default; 0/off/false/no stops that work without a deploy and keeps
# whatever was already written:
# FBI_TEAM_CALENDAR=1     the feed that asks the provider for the list of matches of the teams about to play (F4; part of the day's requests)
# FBI_MATCH_KNOWLEDGE=1   the job that puts a finished match together in layers (F7; database only, no request to the provider)
# FBI_RESETTLE=1          the routine re-settlement of the picks of a match whose result was corrected

# ── Match packets stored only when they change (Plan Maestro PM, PM-13-03; BE-065; docs/owner/PM_13_03_PAQUETES_SIN_REPETIR.md) ──────
# A packet's schedule block carries the age of each side's calendar read (age_hours), so every build had a new hash and a new row of
# ai.match_packets (46.5 % of the new rows on 20-nov-2026 differed from the previous one in those two numbers alone). on: before
# inserting, the packet is compared with its fixture's newest stored one without those two fields; when equal, that row is reused.
# Nothing the AI reads is built differently and nothing stored changes. Off by default; anything not on/1/true/yes is off. Restart the
# worker to read it.
# FBI_PACKET_STORE_STABLE=off

# ── The post-mortem and the memory (plan F8, docs/owner/POSTMORTEM_MEMORIA_F8.md) ────────────────────────
# There is ONE post-mortem of a selection (intel.postmortems, pm-v6). The two first ones - a match's (ai.postmortems) and a selection's
# (ai.pick_postmortems) - are frozen: their tables keep what they wrote and nothing reads them for what is new. FBI_AI_LEGACY_POSTMORTEMS=1
# makes the daily learning cycle write them again beside the new one. It exists to go back, not to be used; the worker needs a restart to
# read it. Off = anything but 1/on/true/yes.
# FBI_AI_LEGACY_POSTMORTEMS=0

# ── The weekly search for patterns (plan F12.6, docs/owner/PATRONES_F12.md) ──────────────────────────────
# Every Monday at 04:40 Bogotá, as the last step of intel_weekly, the settled decisions of the last 90 days are compared group against
# rest (market, line, model, competition, team, referee, coach...) on three measures, and what reaches |z| >= 3 is counted against what
# chance alone would give. It reads the database only: 0 provider requests, 0 AI, and nothing it finds reaches a model, a forecast or a pick.
#   off      the step does not run (the default, and what anything unknown means)
#   report   it runs and keeps a summary in the run's record (intel.runs, counts.patterns); nothing else is written
#   propose  ...and the findings that repeat in both halves of the window (at most 5) are proposed to the owner in Evolución, once each
# The worker needs a restart to read it. The whole reading, any time, on demand: python -m scripts.patterns search
# FBI_PATTERN_SEARCH=off

# ── The families in shadow (plans F10 and F11, docs/owner/FAMILIAS_F10.md and docs/owner/CICLO_FAMILIAS_F11.md) ──────────
# The goals of each half, the corners and the cards have models of their own (F10) and a cycle of their own (F11). Neither reaches a user,
# a pick or a model of the pipeline: what they write is research, under versions of their own. The worker needs a restart to read these.
# FBI_FAMILY_FORECASTS=1 writes their forecasts of the upcoming matches (family-v1) every FBI_FAMILY_FORECAST_MINUTES=180. On by default;
# 0/off/false/no stops it and keeps whatever was written.
# FBI_FAMILY_DECISIONS says what the worker does with those forecasts:
#   off      nothing: the families are not judged, settled or remembered (the default, and what anything unknown means)
#   shadow   one pass of decisions an hour (decision-fam-v1, never above Investigación, stake zero) and, at night, their settlement
#            (outcome-fam-v1), post-mortem (pm-fam-v1) and memory (memory-fam-v1); the post-mortem and the memory need migration 0118.
#            Seen only in Aprendizaje > Familias of the Admin Console. Back to off at any time: what was written stays.
# FBI_FAMILY_DECISIONS=off

# ── Feature sets keyed by the model code, not by the commit (Plan Maestro PM, PM-13-02; BE-064; docs/owner/PM_13_02_RASGOS_SIN_REPETIR.md) ──
# The pick pipeline's forecast stores a fixture's feature set again when its inputs OR its code changed; the code was the commit, so each
# deploy rewrote every upcoming fixture's vector with the same values. on: the code is the first commit that ran the model code in force
# (a deploy that leaves fbi.models/features/predictions/backtesting/domain as they were writes nothing new). Off by default; anything not
# on/1/true/yes is off. Nothing stored changes either way. Restart the worker to read it.
# FBI_FEATURE_SETS_BY_MODEL_CODE=off

# ── Memory of each worker job (Plan Maestro PM, PM-13-05; OPS-010; docs/owner/PM_13_05_MEMORIA_DEL_WORKER.md) ──────────
# A measurement nobody sees: the worker samples its own resident memory every 5 s and writes, per job run, a `job.memory` log
# line and, for ledger runs, raw.ingestion_runs.params._mem. On by default; 0 turns it off (restart the worker).
# FBI_WORKER_MEMWATCH=1

# ── Availability matrix: the nightly recalculation (Plan Maestro PM, PM-02-03; BE-056) ─────────────────────────────────────
# A measurement nobody sees while FBI_AVAILABILITY is off: at 08:00 UTC (again at 08:40 and 11:20 if the first found no room) the
# worker STARTS `python -m scripts.availability_refresh` in a process of its own, capped at 512 MiB and first to go if the container
# runs short, only when the container has 384 MiB free besides its page cache. Incremental each night, full on Sundays; writes only
# analytics.coverage_* (migration 0169) and one row of raw.ingestion_runs (job_type availability_refresh, with its duration and
# memory peak). On by default; 0 turns it off (restart the worker); the rows written stay.
# FBI_AVAILABILITY_REFRESH=1

# ── The market's margin and dispersion by competition and day (Plan Maestro PM, PM-05-07; BE-077) ─────────────────────────────
# A measurement nobody sees: at the end of the nightly process above (scripts.availability_refresh), the margin of each house's
# complete book (sum of 1/price - 1) and the dispersion across houses of the fair probability in 1X2, BTTS and OU 2.5, from
# market.final_prematch_odds, by UTC day of kick-off and competition, into market.league_daily_stats (migration 0170), with one row of
# raw.ingestion_runs (job_type market_league_stats). Nothing reads it to price, pick or decide. OFF while the line is absent;
# =1 turns it on (restart the worker). `python -m scripts.market_league_stats check --day <día>` (read only) recomputes a day.
# FBI_MARKET_LEAGUE_STATS=0

# ── Availability over HTTP: contract C-16 (Plan Maestro PM, PM-02-05; BE-058) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: the five routes (/availability/competitions, /availability/competitions/{id},
# /matches/{id}/availability, /admin/availability/matrix, /admin/availability/changes) answer 404, the private ones too.
# =1 opens them (the API recreated) and, for the owner, the «Disponibilidad» tab of /admin/competitions (PM-02-08, UX-174) and the
# states «información no disponible» where a screen uses them (PM-14-01, UX-173); readers' modules change only when they read the
# matrix (PM-14-04).
# FBI_AVAILABILITY=0
# The cups split by phase (PM-02-07; BE-067): OFF while the line is absent - C-16 answers «todas» only. =1 adds each cup season's
# phase cells (previa, liga_o_grupos, eliminatoria) and grades a cup match's blocks by its own phase (the API recreated). The nightly
# recalculation measures the phases either way (written to analytics.coverage_cells; nothing reads them while this is off).
# FBI_AVAILABILITY_PHASES=0

# ── Availability: the shadow comparison (Plan Maestro PM, PM-02-06; BE-059) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A record nobody sees: after the nightly recalculation, in a process of its own (08:30 UTC, never the worker's; BE-094), once a day, what Mercados (C-14),
# Cuotas, the model's figure and the statistics (C-13) show for 500 matches still to be played against what the matrix would say,
# into analytics.availability_discrepancies (14 days before any module reads the matrix: PM-14-04). On by default; 0 turns it off.
# FBI_AVAILABILITY_SHADOW=1

# ── Colombian tables computed from the rules file (Plan Maestro PM, PM-09-01; BE-075) ────────────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: no reader sees the reclasificación, the relegation table by average or the places computed by
# fbi.competitions.season_tables. They are read only in shadow (python -m scripts.competition_tables show|check, read-only).
# With it on, GET /competitions/{id}/season-tables answers (BE-082) and the competition's page (FBI_COMPETITION_PAGE) draws them.
# It is turned on only after the owner signs the cotejo of the regulation (docs/owner/DOC_008_...) and the publication (DM-14).
# FBI_COMPETITION_TABLES=0

# ── The block «Árbitro designado», BUILT, NOT EXPOSED (Plan Maestro PM, PM-08-02; BE-080) ──────────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent, and no route, page or packet reads it even on: a block about a named person waits for the lawyer's
# answer on Ley 1581 (DM-08). fbi.people.referee_block: cards per match, share of matches with a red card and with a penalty awarded,
# each with n, a 95 % interval and the league's figure, shown only with the matrix at B or better. Read only with
# `python -m scripts.referee_block show --fixture <id>`.
# FBI_REFEREE_BLOCK=0

# ── The difficulty of a team's coming matches, IN SHADOW (Plan Maestro PM, PM-08-05; BE-079) ─────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent, and no route, page or packet reads it even on: the mean Elo of the next five rivals as faced (minus
# the home advantage at home, plus it away) with its 95 % margin can be read as a forecast, so it waits for the owner's publication
# signature (DM-14). Read only with `python -m scripts.schedule_difficulty show|league|check` (formula in fbi.competitions.schedule_difficulty).
# FBI_SCHEDULE_DIFFICULTY=0

# ── The expected table with the provider's xG, IN SHADOW (Plan Maestro PM, PM-09-06; BE-083) ───────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent, and no route, page or packet reads it even on: the points each team would have from the xG of its
# matches (Poisson of mean the xG, «xG de API-Football») can be read as a forecast, so it waits for the owner's publication signature
# (DM-14); only for leagues whose xG the matrix grades B or better. Read only with `python -m scripts.expected_table show|eligible|check`
# (formula in fbi.stats.expected_table; guide docs/owner/PM_09_06_TABLA_ESPERADA_XG.md).
# FBI_EXPECTED_TABLE=0

# ── The models judged by competition and coverage level (Plan Maestro PM, PM-12-06; IA-152) ────────────────────────────────────
# FBI_MODEL_SEGMENTS: OFF while the line is absent. =1: once a week (Mondays) the nightly process of the matrix scores the stored
# forecasts against the results by competition and by the matrix's level (fbi.coverage.model_segments, into analytics.evaluation_reports
# and analytics.evaluation_segments): sample, intervals and the verdict of each competition's own sample. Private; it changes no pick,
# model or forecast. By hand: `python -m scripts.model_segments show|check|verdicts|run` (guide docs/owner/PM_12_06_EVALUACION_POR_COMPETICION.md).
# FBI_MODEL_SEGMENTS=0
# FBI_PROB_BY_COMPETITION: OFF while the line is absent. =1: state 5 of C-16 (behind FBI_AVAILABILITY) also asks the competition's own
# verdict - a market's forecast is authorised there only when the newest weekly report calls it «apta»; a competition with no verdict
# (every new one) reads «no autorizada». No pick, model or forecast reads it. Turn on only with the kit, after a report exists.
# FBI_PROB_BY_COMPETITION=0

# ── The owner's private evaluation board (Plan Maestro PM, PM-12-01; IA-153) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: GET /admin/evaluation/board answers 404, the Performance page shows no panel and the weekly batch
# computes no board. =1: once a week (Mondays, the nightly process of the matrix) the board of the last whole week is computed
# (fbi.coverage.weekly_board: PrediGol's forecast, the market and the provider on the same matches; Brier split into reliability
# and resolution; paired differences with intervals) into analytics.evaluation_reports, and the owner sees it with the report by
# competition (PM-12-06). Not a proof of an edge; it changes no pick, model or forecast. By hand: `python -m scripts.evaluation_board
# show|run` (guide docs/owner/PM_12_01_TABLERO_EVALUACION.md).
# FBI_EVALUATION_BOARD=0

# ── The facts of a match's «importance» (Plan Maestro PM, PM-05-08; BE-078) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: nothing a reader sees reads them. fbi.competitions.importance says, as of a moment and as facts (never
# a probability), the stage of a match, its match day with the days and matches left in the published schedule, and the home side's
# place among the home records (the away side's among the away records) of the stored table taken before kick-off. Read only with
# `python -m scripts.match_importance show --fixture <id>`. The fact sheet of the chronicle and the competition's page carry them when
# this is turned on (audited kit, with the Intelligence session).
# FBI_MATCH_IMPORTANCE_FACTS=0

# ── Statistics: what the provider measured and no page showed (Plan Maestro PM, PM-05-05; BE-068) ─────────────────────────────
# OFF by default (the statistics documents are then exactly what they were). =1: the nightly statistics pass (FBI_STATS_AGG, 07:20
# UTC) adds to each team's and player's document `provider_extras` (C-13 1.1.0): a player's offsides, dribbled past, penalties won,
# committed and saved, a team's offsides - each with its sample, its coverage and its origin («dato de API-Football»). The first night
# rewrites every document once. Goals prevented has its own switch, on only after `python -m scripts.goals_prevented_probe` says PASS.
# FBI_STATS_PROVIDER_EXTRAS=0
# FBI_STATS_GOALS_PREVENTED=0

# ── The Match Center's shot funnel and its two zones (Plan Maestro PM, PM-10-01, lámina I01; FE-005) ───────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: Estadísticas is as it was. =1 draws «Embudo de remate» and «Zona de remate · 2 zonas» at the top of
# the tab once a match is under way, only where the team statistics are of level B or better (C-16, when FBI_AVAILABILITY answers)
# and the match delivered every figure (the API recreated). It reads the match detail; no new query.
# FBI_MATCH_SHOT_FUNNEL=0

# ── The Match Center's balance and strip of the score's state (Plan Maestro PM, PM-10-02, lámina I01; FE-006) ──────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: Estadísticas is as it was. =1 draws «Balanza del partido» (level B or better of team statistics) and
# «Estado del marcador» of a finished match (where the events are; level C shows it alone) at the top of the tab (the API recreated).
# It reads the match detail; no new query.
# FBI_MATCH_BALANCE=0

# ── The data layers of the line-up pitch (Plan Maestro PM, PM-10-04, lámina I02; UX-176) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: Alineaciones is as it was. =1 puts the choice of layers (rating, minutes, cards, goals and assists) on
# the pitch where the player statistics are of level B or better (C-16, when FBI_AVAILABILITY answers) and every starter has his
# line (the API recreated). It reads the match detail; no new query.
# FBI_LINEUP_LAYERS=0

# ── The Match Center by coverage level (Plan Maestro PM, PM-14-02, láminas I01 and I04; UX-177) ───────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: the six tabs and the blocks as always. =1 (with FBI_AVAILABILITY=1, which it reads) leaves out the tabs
# that would open on nothing in the competition, shows in Estadísticas what a competition without team statistics does deliver (facts
# of the match sheet, one note, form and table) and notes partial odds (the API recreated). Turn it on only after the shadow comparison
# of PM-02-06 (FBI_AVAILABILITY_SHADOW, 21-nov to 4-dic) shows no unexplained discrepancy.
# FBI_MATCH_COVERAGE=0

# ── The result forecast in 100 icons, with «Mito o dato» (Plan Maestro PM, PM-10-07, lámina I09; UX-182) ─────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: «Pronóstico PrediGol» is as it was. =1 offers «Barras | Iconos» on the result market (1X2) where it is
# calibrated with a validated calibrator and readers may see it (the API recreated). It counts the figure the bars show: no new number,
# no new query.
# FBI_PROB_ICONS=0

# ── The owner's console of the provider's requests (Plan Maestro PM, PM-04-05; BE-076, UX-175) ────────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: GET /admin/monitoring/provider-usage answers 404 and /admin/operation shows no «Consumo del
# proveedor» view. =1 opens both (the API recreated). It reads raw.provider_quota, raw.provider_endpoint_usage and
# raw.ingestion_payloads; it asks the provider nothing.
# FBI_USAGE_CONSOLE=0

# ── Readers' pages of plan PM, wave 4 (PM-09-04, PM-09-05, PM-08-06, PM-09-03; UX-178 to UX-181, BE-082) ─────────────────────────
# All OFF while the line is absent; =1 opens each (the API recreated). They read routes readers already have and C-16
# (FBI_AVAILABILITY) where it is on; nothing is estimated. Turned on in order in PM-15-03, with an audited kit.
# A competition's page (/competitions/<id>): tables, calendar and results, leaders and coverage level.
# FBI_COMPETITION_PAGE=0
# The world directory of competitions with level and priority (/competitions): needs FBI_AVAILABILITY to show anything.
# FBI_COMPETITION_DIRECTORY=0
# The player's profile with the new data (goalkeeper and outfield player): reads C-13's provider_extras (FBI_STATS_PROVIDER_EXTRAS).
# FBI_PLAYER_PROFILE_EXTRAS=0
# The calculator «¿Qué pasa si…?» under the season tables (needs FBI_COMPETITION_TABLES): only with the owner's signature (DM-14).
# FBI_WHAT_IF=0

# ── Switches of the plan de correcciones UX (23-nov-2026): all born OFF ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One Inicio for everyone, with the «Tus favoritos» strip (plan de correcciones UX, AP-I01, decision D1). The UX session turns it on after verifying it (D1 is approved).
# FBI_HOME_UNIFIED=0
# A match's markets as a bookmaker lays them out (plan de correcciones UX, AP-P08, decision D6). The UX session turns it on after verifying it.
# FBI_MARKETS_V3=0
# «Lo más interesante de hoy» on days without picks (plan de correcciones UX, AP-K04, decision D2). The UX session turns it on after verifying it.
# FBI_DAY_HIGHLIGHTS=0
# «Mis casas»: the bookmakers the reader plays at, in Perfil, Mercados and Cuotas (plan de correcciones UX, AP-P10, decision D5). Only the owner turns it on, after the lawyer's answer.
# FBI_MY_BOOKS=0
# Variable units on picks, parlays, Mis picks and Transparencia (plan de correcciones UX, AP-K07, decision D3). Only the owner turns it on, when contract C-17 is active with calibrated models.
# FBI_STAKES=0
# The parlay builder «Por tendencias» (plan de correcciones UX, AP-L02, decision D7). Only the owner turns it on, after Intelligence validates contract C-18.
# FBI_TREND_BUILDER=0
# The e-mails in the brand's layout - header, card, a tone for each kind, 44 px button, dark version - with the same words (plan de correcciones UX, AP-M01, decision D13). The messenger and the API read it (recreate both). The UX session turns it on after sending a test to the owner's account.
# FBI_EMAIL_V2=0

# ── The subscribable calendar of the teams a reader follows (Plan Maestro PM, PM-14-06, OP-43; BE-084) ─────────────────────────────
# OFF while the line is absent: /me/calendar-feed and the secret links /calendar/feed/<secret>.ics answer 404. =1 opens them (the API
# recreated). A link is a 256-bit secret kept only as its SHA-256 (customer.calendar_feeds), read-only, revocable, with the fixtures of
# the followed teams and nothing else. Turned on ONLY after the security review is approved by the security session and the owner
# (docs/owner/BE_084_REVISION_SEGURIDAD_CALENDARIO.md), with Caddy's access log filtering the secret out first.
# FBI_CALENDAR_FEED=0
